WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.780
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Rules Have Reasons.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:17.560
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.429
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:20.429 --> 00:00:23.297
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:23.297 --> 00:00:29.033
Our classroom has rules. Every classroom does.

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:37.637
Here is a secret about rules: a good rule is never just floating there. It is standing on a reason.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:46.242
If you look under a rule, you can usually find the reason holding it up.

00:00:46.242 --> 00:00:50.066
Let's look under three rules together.

00:00:50.066 --> 00:00:58.670
We walk inside. The reason: bodies stay safe. Running feet and small spaces do not mix.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:07.275
We take turns and share. The reason: turns stay fair. Everyone gets a real chance.

00:01:07.275 --> 00:01:15.879
We keep our voices low while others work. The reason: learning stays possible. Ears need room to think.

00:01:15.879 --> 00:01:21.615
Safe bodies. Fair turns. Room to learn. That is what the rules are carrying.

00:01:21.615 --> 00:01:24.483
And some rules protect people you cannot see — the class after us, the little kids, the person who cleans our floor.

00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:32.132
Sometimes a rule feels unfair. That feeling is allowed. Here is the move for it.

00:01:32.132 --> 00:01:40.736
Ask a grown-up why. Calmly. "Can you tell me the reason for this rule?"

00:01:40.736 --> 00:01:46.472
Then listen to the whole answer — not just the first word of it.

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:49.340
Grown-ups can explain. And a rule with a reason you understand is a rule you can stand behind.

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:56.033
Rules have reasons. Reasons can be asked for, and reasons can be heard.

00:01:56.033 --> 00:02:00.813
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:00.813 --> 00:02:04.637
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:04.637 --> 00:02:09.417
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:09.417 --> 00:02:14.197
You're ready for what's next.
